            <div xml:id="d764">

                <pb facs="0838" n="739" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg739"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.00/3465: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Third Secretary of Embassy in Spain</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Wendelin</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-10-15T13:00:00+00:00">October 15, 1936—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 15—11:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>X–217. My telegram No. X–122, September 4, 3 p.m. <hi rendition="#italic">Note
                        verbale</hi> just received from Foreign Office encloses copy of official
                    reports of activities Government Air Forces based on airfields in South namely
                    Alcazares (Cartagena), Almeria, Valencia, Guadix (Cordoba front) and Malaga on
                    August 30, last. None of operations reported included area near where destroyer
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Kane</hi> was attacked.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wendelin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
